notes=r'''Manuscript page 13 is enclosed by a curved stroke at the upper right; the lower-left number is 15. This page completes the Proposition begun on scan 015. It adds that the homomorphism sends the distinguished projectors to the grading projectors, with the oval margin warning “condition essentielle !”. It asserts uniqueness and the images of the lowering operator and component operators. The slanted margin supplies conditions (iii) and (iv), absent from H, with an underlined réalisation and an unresolved Φ|Θ. Two long strokes cross that margin; its status is marked doubtful in place and both strokes are reproduced. The proof has a large cancelled attempt to recover the degree projectors, followed by a live argument using two endpoint identities and a final appeal to (6.14).

**N16-016-C1 — cancelled degree-shift identity.** The cancelled identity visibly has π′_(i+α), matching both drafts. In the n=1 matrices of N16-015-R1, set i=0 and α=1. Then LP_0=L, whereas P_1L=0. The formula with i+α fails even in this concrete exterior example. **N16-016-R1** is the exact degree identity with i+2α: on x of degree r, L^απ_i x=δ_(r,i)L^αx and π_(i+2α)L^αx=δ_(r+2α,i+2α)L^αx. The deltas agree, proving the corrected identity degree by degree. The cancelled source formula is preserved.

**N16-016-P1 — why the added projector condition matters, by an explicit morphism.** Use Φ_0 at n=1 with the block isomorphism Mat_2(Z)⊕Z established in N16-015-R1. The projection (A,c)↦c is a unital graded-ring morphism to Z concentrated in degree zero; it sends L_0 to 0. Represent this target on M^0=Z with every other M^i=0, still with n=1. The operator L=0 has no inverse from M^0 to M^2, so the Lefschetz condition fails. The morphism sends the source π_0 to 0, while the target grading projector π_0 is 1. Thus this concrete morphism satisfies the operator-image requirement alone and violates the added projector-image requirement. It gives exact content to the author’s “condition essentielle !” without removing that insertion.

**N16-016-C2 — the displayed source endpoint identities in the integral exterior construction.** In the n=2 example of N16-014-C1/C2, L²(1)=2v, C(v)=ξ and Cξ=2. Hence C²L²(1)=4. The displayed source expression (C²L²−1)π_0 sends 1 to 3. At the other end, L²C²(v)=4v, so (L²C²−1)π_4 sends v to 3v. Both alleged zero relations fail in the source construction with raw contraction. **N16-016-R2** records the exact replacement on this explicit rational chain: C=2B, hence C²L²=4B²L² and L²C²=4L²B²; B²L²π_0=π_0 and L²B²π_4=π_4. The source zero relations are not silently repaired. The general Proposition is not certified by the present proof because these stated source premises fail in its integral example.

**N16-016-P2 — transport of the written expression.** For the particular morphism φ specified in (ii), its defining properties give φ((bold Λ_0^(n−i) bold L_0^(n−i)−1)bold π_i)=(φ(bold Λ_0)^(n−i)L^(n−i)−1)π_i, directly by preservation of multiplication, addition and 1; the same expansion applies to the second expression. This checks the algebraic transport itself and does not certify that either source expression is zero. The ink supplies a prime on each Λ′ in the transferred identities; H omits both. The definition of Λ′ and the later uniqueness formula write bold Λ without a separate 0; the first prose occurrence has an ambiguous small loop fused with its foot, now marked Λ_0|Λ.

The uniqueness passage has a live inserted equality for the images of π_(i,α), which H strikes out. Its adjective is simultanée and attaches to caractérisation. The final reference (6.14) is legible despite reinforcement. The earlier checks on scans 012–013 already record problems in the written global formulas and ranges, so this reference is preserved without certifying all those formulas. The small cancelled fragment below Pour φ(Λ is retained as a doubtful π_(i,α); neither witness supplied it. No closing parenthesis is supplied after that abandoned Λ because none is visible. The heavily crossed opening word, quelque, older indices, two property/relation phrases, pour ceci and donc on a remain uncertain.'''
